l copies, notes, and derivatives thereof, and shall, upon request, certify in writing that it has done so. Notwithstanding the foregoing, the Receiving Party may retain one copy solely for legal or compliance archival purposes, subject to continuing confidentiality obligations.7. No License or Rights GrantedNothing in this Agreement shall be construed as granting the Receiving Party any license, right, title, or interest in or to any Confidential Information, patent, copyright, trademark, trade secret, or other intellectual property of the Disclosing Party, whether by implication, estoppel, or otherwise. All Confidential Information remains the sole and exclusive property of the Disclosing Party.8. No WarrantyAll Confidential Information is provided "AS IS." Each Disclosing Party makes no representations or warranties, express or implied, as to the accuracy or completeness of the Confidential Information, and shall have no liability to the Receiving Party resulting from its use of the Confidential Information.9. MiscellaneousAmendments. No amendment or modification of this Agreement shall be effective unless made in writing and signed by both Parties.No Waiver. The failure of either party to enforce any provision of this Agreement shall not constitute a waiver of that or any other provision.10. AcceptanceIN WITNESS WHEREOF, the Parties have executed this Agreement as of the Effective Date.Sample 1SignatureName: Sample 24Title: Sample 25DateSample 3SignatureName: Sample 26Title: Sample 27DateDisclaimer: This tool generates a general-purpose NDA and is not legal advice. Have it reviewed by an attorney for your specific situation and state.







